---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const contact = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL || 'curatedpick.store@gmail.com';
---
<Layout title="Privacy policy — The Curated Pick" description="Privacy policy for The Curated Pick affiliate product discovery website.">
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY POLICY</p>
    <h1>Your privacy, kept simple.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Last updated: September 25, 2026</p>
    <p>The Curated Pick is an affiliate product-discovery website. You can browse product pages without creating an account, signing in, or giving us personal information.</p>

    <h2>Information we receive</h2>
    <p>When you browse, our hosting and security providers may process technical information such as your IP address, browser type, device information, and requested pages. This is used to deliver and protect the site.</p>
    <p>Search terms and filters run in your browser. We do not use advertising pixels or a third-party analytics profile on this site.</p>

    <h2>Product links and affiliate partners</h2>
    <p>Product pages contain links to stores such as Amazon, AliExpress, Alibaba, and other merchants. Those stores and affiliate networks may use cookies or similar tools to attribute a visit or qualifying purchase. Their own privacy policies control what they collect after you leave this site. See our <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

    <h2>Pinterest</h2>
    <p>We may publish product links to our Pinterest account through Pinterest's official API. Pinterest account authorization is used only for that publishing connection. Visitors to this website are not asked to connect a Pinterest account, and we do not collect Pinterest passwords. Pinterest's privacy policy applies to activity on Pinterest.</p>

    <h2>Images and hosting</h2>
    <p>Product images and catalog data may be delivered from our hosting or Supabase storage. These providers may process technical request information needed to serve the files.</p>

    <h2>Optional AI suggestions for editors</h2>
    <p>Editors may choose to send a product title and poster image to Google's Gemini API to suggest a description, category, and tags. These suggestions are optional and reviewed by an editor before publication. When using Google's unpaid API tier, Google may use submitted content to improve its services and human reviewers may process it. Do not send private or sensitive material. See <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Gemini API terms</a>.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we receive the information you choose to include and use it to reply. Do not send passwords, payment details, or other sensitive information. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can clear local browser storage to remove saved display preferences. You can also block cookies or leave the site before opening a merchant link. We do not control the privacy practices of external services.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy when the site or its services change. The date above shows when the latest version was published.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
